From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eriko Kurimoto <elkurin@google.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 08:37:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 21/48] [FileChooser]: Mitigate spoofing in small windows

File pickers and directory enumerations could previously be triggered or
kept open inside very small or hidden windows where browser UI context
is obscured, enabling UI spoofing attacks.

Require a minimum top-level window size (400x300) and visible
WebContents state before showing file pickers or directory enumerations,
and cancel active file chooser dialogs if the top-level window shrinks
below the minimum threshold. Checking top-level window bounds instead of
WebContents bounds avoids false positives when a tab's content area is
narrowed by side panels, DevTools, or split view panes.

Consolidate the size check and resize cancellation logic into
content::WebContentsBasedCanceller in content/public/browser/ so both
chrome/ and content/ share the same predicate, constants, and observer
logic. Add a base::Feature killswitch (FileChooserMinWindowSize), UMA
histograms (Content.FileChooser.SuppressedByWindowSize,
SuppressedWindowWidth, SuppressedWindowHeight), and a DevTools console
warning when a file chooser is suppressed.

